            <h2 class="TextThreeXLElement FontBoldElement TrackingTightElement TextGrayNineHundredElement SmallTextFourXLElement">A Design Process with Clear Priorities</h2>
            <p class="MarginTSixElement TextLargeElement LeadingEightElement TextGraySixHundredElement">Every home has its own rhythms, constraints and character. A thoughtful design conversation begins by understanding those details instead of assuming that one approach will suit everyone. This helps bring practical needs and visual preferences into the same discussion.</p>
            <p class="MarginTSixElement TextLargeElement LeadingEightElement TextGraySixHundredElement">Rather than presenting unverified company figures, this section describes four useful parts of an interior design conversation. They are prompts for shaping a project, not claims about completed work, client numbers, measured results or guaranteed outcomes. The right emphasis will depend on the space and the priorities you share.</p>
          </div>
